-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Commute To Move Back Chain Family Zero
-- statement:
--   **The commuted endpoint is qSDD-close to the first move-back family.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a quantum state on `ι x ι`, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, let `zeta` be an error, and let `r` be a natural number. Assume the slice-level self-consistency relation
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}\!\left(\psi_{bi},\operatorname{Unif}(\operatorname{SliceQuestion}(\mathrm{params})),
--   \operatorname{gHatSelfConsistencyLeftFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family}),
--   \operatorname{gHatSelfConsistencyRightFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family}),
--   \operatorname{gHatSelfConsistencyError}(\zeta)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then, on the move-chain question distribution `MoveQ(params,r+1)`, the commuted family at length `r+1` is related at the same error to the zero-index member of the move-back chain:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}\!\left(\psi_{bi},\operatorname{Unif}(\operatorname{MoveQ}(\mathrm{params},r+1)),
--   \operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_commuteFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r+1),
--   \operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_moveBackChainFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r,0),
--   \operatorname{gHatSelfConsistencyError}(\zeta)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the first edge used after the forward move chain when the leading completed-slice factor is brought back through the product.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_commute_to_moveBackChainFamily_zero`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/CommuteGHalfSandwich/MoveChain/BackChain.lean#L107-L201

